    "| 3 | Operations & ufuncs | 03.03 | Computing derived indicators |\n",
    "| 4 | Missing values | 03.04 | Handling reporting gaps |\n",
    "| 5 | Hierarchical indexing | 03.05 | Multi-dimensional sector analysis |\n",
    "| 6 | Concat & append | 03.06 | Combining quarterly reports |\n",
    "| 7 | Merge & join | 03.07 | Integrating multi-source indicators |\n",
    "| 8 | Aggregation & grouping | 03.08 | Regional comparative analysis |\n",
    "| 9 | Pivot tables | 03.09 | Executive summary dashboards |\n",
    "| 10 | String operations | 03.10 | Cleaning messy country/sector names |\n",
    "| 11 | Time series | 03.11 | Econometric trend analysis |\n",
    "| 12 | Performance eval/query | 03.12 | Large-scale economic datasets |\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup — Imports & Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.width', 120)\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.float_format', '{:.2f}'.format)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Pandas version: {pd.__version__}')\n",
    "print(f'NumPy version:  {np.__version__}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 1: Foundations — Building Economic DataFrames\n",
    "\n",
    "**Scenario:** We are analysts at an international economic observatory. Our task is to build a comprehensive dashboard tracking GDP, unemployment, inflation, and trade balance across major economies (2018–2023).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Introducing Pandas Objects* (03.01) — Series, DataFrame, Index"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 Create the Master Countries Table"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Build master country metadata (Chapter 03.01: DataFrame from dict) ──\n",
    "countries_data = {\n",
    "    'country':            ['USA', 'China', 'Japan', 'Germany', 'UK', 'France', 'Italy', 'Brazil'],\n",
    "    'continent':          ['North America', 'Asia', 'Asia', 'Europe', 'Europe',\n",
    "                           'Europe', 'Europe', 'South America'],\n",
    "    'population_millions':[331, 1439, 126, 83, 67, 67, 60, 212],\n",
    "    'gdp_per_capita_2023':[76000, 12500, 39000, 51000, 45000, 41000, 35000, 8900]\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "df_countries = pd.DataFrame(countries_data)\n",
    "df_countries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Generate Multi-Year Economic Indicator DataFrames\n",
    "\n",
    "Each indicator lives in its own DataFrame — a realistic scenario where GDP, unemployment, inflation, and trade data arrive from separate sources."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "years = list(range(2018, 2024))\n",
    "countries_list = df_countries['country'].tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pre-seeded realistic values for key economies (rest is random)\n",
    "gdp_seed = {\n",
    "    'USA':     [2.9, 2.3, 2.1, -2.8, 5.9, 2.5],\n",
    "    'China':   [6.7, 6.0, 2.2, 3.0, 3.0, 5.2],\n",
    "    'Japan':   [0.3, 0.7, -0.3, -0.7, 1.0, 1.9],\n",
    "}\n",
    "unemp_seed = {\n",
    "    'USA':     [3.9, 3.7, 8.1, 5.4, 3.6, 3.7],\n",
    "    'France':  [7.8, 8.4, 8.0, 7.9, 7.4, 7.3],\n",
    "}\n",
    "infl_seed = {\n",
    "    'USA':     [2.4, 1.8, 1.3, 6.8, 4.1, 3.4],\n",
    "    'Germany': [1.7, 1.4, 0.5, 3.1, 6.9, 4.2],\n",
    "}\n",
    "trade_seed = {\n",
    "    'USA':     [-532, -506, -678, -791, -757, -773],\n",
    "    'China':   [591, 422, 535, 668, 823, 823],\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "gdp_records, unemp_records, infl_records, trade_records = [], [], [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "for country in countries_list:\n",
    "    for i, yr in enumerate(years):\n",
    "        gdp   = gdp_seed.get(country, [round(np.random.uniform(-1, 4), 2)] * len(years))[i]\n",
    "        unemp = unemp_seed.get(country, [round(np.random.uniform(3, 10), 1)] * len(years))[i]\n",
    "    infl  = infl_seed.get(country, [round(np.random.uniform(1, 5), 2)] * len(years))[i]\n",
    "        trade = trade_seed.get(country, [round(np.random.uniform(-500, 500), 0)] * len(years))[i]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        gdp_records.append(   {'country': country, 'year': yr, 'gdp_growth': gdp})\n",
    "        unemp_records.append({'country': country, 'year': yr, 'unemployment': unemp})\n",
    "        infl_records.append( {'country': country, 'year': yr, 'inflation': infl})\n",
    "        trade_records.append({'country': country, 'year': yr, 'trade_balance': trade})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_gdp   = pd.DataFrame(gdp_records)\n",
    "df_unemp = pd.DataFrame(unemp_records)\n",
    "df_infl  = pd.DataFrame(infl_records)\n",
    "df_trade = pd.DataFrame(trade_records)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'GDP DataFrame:          {df_gdp.shape[0]} rows × {df_gdp.shape[1]} cols')\n",
    "print(f'Unemployment DataFrame: {df_unemp.shape[0]} rows × {df_unemp.shape[1]} cols')\n",
    "print(f'Inflation DataFrame:    {df_infl.shape[0]} rows × {df_infl.shape[1]} cols')\n",
    "print(f'Trade DataFrame:        {df_trade.shape[0]} rows × {df_trade.shape[1]} cols')\n",
    "df_gdp.head(12)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Insight ▸** In real-world economics, indicators are published by different agencies on different schedules. Building separate DataFrames mirrors this reality and sets up our later `merge` exercises."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 2: Intermediate — Indexing, Selection & Cleaning\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Data Indexing and Selection* (03.02), *Operating on Data* (03.03), *Handling Missing Data* (03.04)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Indexing Patterns for Economic Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Column selection ──\n",
    "print('▼ Column selection:')\n",
    "print(df_gdp[['country', 'gdp_growth']].head())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Boolean masking: identify recession periods ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Recession periods (GDP growth < 0):')\n",
    "recessions = df_gdp[df_gdp['gdp_growth'] < 0]\n",
    "print(recessions.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Multi-condition filtering ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ USA positive-growth years:')\n",
    "print(df_gdp[(df_gdp['country']=='USA') & (df_gdp['gdp_growth']>0)].to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── loc for label-based access ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ loc: China GDP series')\n",
    "print(df_gdp.loc[df_gdp['country']=='China', ['year','gdp_growth']].to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── iloc for positional access ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ iloc: first 5 rows, all columns')\n",
    "print(df_gdp.iloc[:5])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 Operations — Computing Derived Economic Indicators\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Operating on Data in Pandas* (03.03) — UFuncs, index alignment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Merge GDP + unemployment first so we can compute derived metrics ──\n",
    "df_macro = pd.merge(df_gdp, df_unemp, on=['country','year'])\n",
    "df_macro = pd.merge(df_macro, df_infl, on=['country','year'])\n",
    "df_macro = pd.merge(df_macro, df_trade, on=['country','year'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Misery Index = unemployment + inflation (Arthur Okun, 1970s) ──\n",
    "df_macro['misery_index'] = df_macro['unemployment'] + df_macro['inflation']\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Real GDP growth proxy = nominal growth - inflation ──\n",
    "df_macro['real_growth_proxy'] = df_macro['gdp_growth'] - df_macro['inflation']\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Trade-to-GDP ratio surrogate (trade openness indicator) ──\n",
    "#    Using |trade_balance| / (gdp_growth + 100) * 100 as a rough openness score\n",
    "df_macro['trade_openness'] = df_macro['trade_balance'].abs() / (df_macro['gdp_growth'].abs() + 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Derived indicators added: misery_index, real_growth_proxy, trade_openness')\n",
    "df_macro[df_macro['country']=='USA'].to_string(index=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Insight ▸** The **Misery Index** (unemployment + inflation) is a widely cited political-economic barometer. Pandas' vectorized arithmetic makes such composite indicators trivial to compute."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3 Handling Missing Values in Economic Data\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Handling Missing Data* (03.04) — `isnull`, `dropna`, `fillna`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Inject realistic missing-data patterns ──\n",
    "df_missing = df_macro.copy()\n",
    "df_missing.loc[3, 'gdp_growth']    = np.nan   # delayed GDP publication\n",
    "df_missing.loc[10, 'unemployment'] = np.nan   # missing labor survey\n",
    "df_missing.loc[20, 'inflation']    = np.nan   # suppressed CPI data\n",
    "df_missing.loc[30, 'trade_balance']= np.nan   # customs delay\n",
    "\n",
    "print('▼ Missing value count by column:')\n",
    "print(df_missing.isnull().sum())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Strategy 1: Drop rows with ANY missing data (strict — loses data)\n",
    "dropped = df_missing.dropna()\n",
    "print(f'\\nDrop strategy: {len(dropped)} rows retained (lost {len(df_missing)-len(dropped)})')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Strategy 2: Forward-fill (common for time series — carry last known value)\n",
    "df_ffill = df_missing.sort_values(['country','year']).copy()\n",
    "df_ffill[['gdp_growth','unemployment','inflation','trade_balance']] = (\n",
    "    df_ffill.groupby('country')[['gdp_growth','unemployment','inflation','trade_balance']]\n",
    "           .fillna(method='ffill')\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Forward-fill result for Italy (where row 20 was NaN):')\n",
    "print(df_ffill[df_ffill['country']=='Italy'][['year','inflation']].to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Strategy 3: Group-mean imputation (most balanced for cross-sectional data)\n",
    "df_imputed = df_missing.copy()\n",
    "for col in ['gdp_growth','unemployment','inflation','trade_balance']:\n",
    "    df_imputed[col] = df_imputed.groupby('country')[col].transform(\n",
    "        lambda s: s.fillna(s.mean())\n",
    "    )\n",
    "print(f'\\nGroup-mean imputation — remaining NaNs: {df_imputed.isnull().sum().sum()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Insight ▸** The choice of missing-value strategy has real economic consequences. Forward-fill assumes persistence (valid for GDP), while group-mean imputation assumes cross-sectional similarity (valid for inflation among peer economies)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 3: Advanced Integration — Merge, Concat, Hierarchical Indexing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Hierarchical Indexing* (03.05), *Concat & Append* (03.06), *Merge & Join* (03.07)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.1 Merge — Joining Indicators with Policy Metadata"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Trade-agreement metadata (a separate dataset) ──\n",
    "trade_agreements = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'country':         ['USA','China','Japan','Germany','UK','France','Mexico','Canada'],\n",
    "    'agreement':       ['USMCA','RCEP','CPTPP','EU Single Market','EU Single Market',\n",
    "                        'EU Single Market','USMCA','USMCA'],\n",
    "    'membership_year': [2020, 2020, 2022, 1993, 1973, 1973, 2020, 2020]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left join: keep ALL economic data, attach agreement info where available\n",
    "df_policy = pd.merge(df_macro, trade_agreements, on='country', how='left')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('▼ Left join — economic data enriched with trade-agreement metadata:')\n",
    "cols = ['country','year','gdp_growth','agreement','membership_year']\n",
    "print(df_policy[cols].head(12).to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Inner join: only countries present in BOTH datasets\n",
    "df_inner = pd.merge(df_macro, trade_agreements, on='country', how='inner')\n",
    "print(f'\\nInner join retained {len(df_inner)} rows (countries in both datasets)')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Which countries were dropped?\n",
    "dropped_countries = set(df_macro['country']) - set(trade_agreements['country'])\n",
    "print(f'Countries without agreement data: {dropped_countries}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Concat — Stacking Quarterly Reports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Two quarterly datasets that need to be stacked ──\n",
    "q_2022 = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'quarter': ['Q1 2022','Q2 2022','Q3 2022','Q4 2022'],\n",
    "    'consumer_spending_b': [14500, 15200, 14800, 15500],\n",
    "    'business_investment_b': [3200, 3500, 3100, 3700]\n",
    "})\n",
    "q_2023 = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'quarter': ['Q1 2023','Q2 2023','Q3 2023','Q4 2023'],\n",
    "    'consumer_spending_b': [15800, 16000, 15900, 16400],\n",
    "    'business_investment_b': [3800, 4100, 3600, 4200]\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Vertical concatenation (stack rows)\n",
    "df_quarterly = pd.concat([q_2022, q_2023], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "df_quarterly['total_demand_b'] = df_quarterly['consumer_spending_b'] + df_quarterly['business_investment_b']\n",
    "\n",
    "print('▼ Concatenated quarterly demand series:')\n",
    "print(df_quarterly.to_string(index=False))\n",
    "\n",
    "# With source labels\n",
    "df_quarterly_tagged = pd.concat([\n",
    "    q_2022.assign(source='FY2022'),\n",
    "    q_2023.assign(source='FY2023')\n",
    "], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Tagged with fiscal year source:')\n",
    "print(df_quarterly_tagged.to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.3 Hierarchical (MultiIndex) — Sector-Level Economic Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Sector × Year hierarchical data ──\n",
    "sectors = ['Technology','Manufacturing','Finance','Agriculture','Services']\n",
    "years_h = [2021, 2022, 2023]\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(99)\n",
    "idx = pd.MultiIndex.from_product([sectors, years_h], names=['Sector','Year'])\n",
    "\n",
    "df_sector = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'revenue_billions':  np.random.uniform(200, 800, len(idx)),\n",
    "    'employment_thousands': np.random.uniform(50, 400, len(idx)),\n",
    "    'growth_pct':       np.random.uniform(-3, 12, len(idx)),\n",
    "}, index=idx)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('▼ MultiIndex DataFrame (Sector → Year):')\n",
    "print(df_sector.round(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Partial indexing — all years for one sector\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Partial slice — Technology sector across all years:')\n",
    "print(df_sector.loc['Technology'].round(1))\n",
    "\n",
    # Cross-section — all sectors for one year\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Cross-section (xs) — 2023 across all sectors:')\n",
    "print(df_sector.xs(2023, level='Year').round(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Aggregate at sector level\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Mean revenue by sector (level=0 aggregation):')\n",
    "print(df_sector.groupby(level=0)['revenue_billions'].mean().round(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Swap levels for alternative view\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Swapped index (Year → Sector), 2021 only:')\n",
    "print(df_sector.swaplevel().loc[2021].round(1))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Insight ▸** Hierarchical indexing lets us represent inherently multi-dimensional economic data (sector × time × indicator) in a 2-D DataFrame. This is the backbone of panel-data analysis in economics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 4: Aggregation, Grouping & Pivot Tables\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Aggregation and Grouping* (03.08), *Pivot Tables* (03.09)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.1 GroupBy — Comparative Economic Analysis"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_analysis = df_macro.copy()\n",
    "df_analysis['continent'] = df_analysis['country'].map({\n",
    "    'USA':'North America','China':'Asia','Japan':'Asia','Germany':'Europe',\n",
    "    'UK':'Europe','France':'Europe','Italy':'Europe','Brazil':'South America'\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Multi-aggregate by continent ──\n",
    "print('▼ Continent-level summary:')\n",
    "continent_agg = df_analysis.groupby('continent').agg({\n",
    "    'gdp_growth':    ['mean','std','min','max'],\n",
    "    'unemployment':  ['mean','max'],\n",
    "    'inflation':     ['mean','max'],\n",
    "    'trade_balance': 'mean'\n",
    "}).round(2)\n",
    "print(continent_agg.to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Year-over-year global trend ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Global GDP growth trend by year:')\n",
    "year_trend = df_analysis.groupby('year')['gdp_growth'].agg(['mean','std','count']).round(2)\n",
    "print(year_trend.to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Country ranking by average GDP growth ──\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Countries ranked by mean GDP growth (descending):')\n",
    "country_rank = df_analysis.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].mean().sort_values(ascending=False).round(2)\n",
    "print(country_rank.to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Filter: keep only countries whose avg unemployment < 6% ──\n",
    "low_unemp = df_analysis.groupby('country').filter(lambda g: g['unemployment'].mean() < 6)\n",
    "print(f'\\n▼ Countries with avg unemployment < 6%: {low_unemp[\"country\"].unique().tolist()}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Transform: z-score normalisation within each country ──\n",
    "df_analysis['gdp_zscore'] = df_analysis.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: (x - x.mean()) / x.std()\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Z-scored GDP growth for Germany:')\n",
    "print(df_analysis[df_analysis['country']=='Germany'][['year','gdp_growth','gdp_zscore']].round(3).to_string(index=False))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Pivot Tables — Executive Dashboards"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── GDP growth: country × year matrix ──\n",
    "pivot_gdp = df_analysis.pivot_table(\n",
    "    values='gdp_growth', index='country', columns='year',\n",
    "    aggfunc='mean', margins=True, margins_name='Mean'\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('▼ GDP Growth (%) — Country × Year:')\n",
    "print(pivot_gdp.round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Misery Index: continent × year ──\n",
    "pivot_misery = df_analysis.pivot_table(\n",
    "    values='misery_index', index='continent', columns='year',\n",
    "    aggfunc='mean', margins=True, margins_name='Overall'\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Misery Index — Continent × Year:')\n",
    "print(pivot_misery.round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Development-level bins ──\n",
    "df_analysis['growth_class'] = pd.cut(\n",
    "    df_analysis['gdp_growth'],\n",
    "    bins=[-np.inf, 0, 2, 4, np.inf],\n",
    "    labels=['Recession','Slow','Moderate','Fast']\n",
    ")\n",
    "pivot_class = df_analysis.pivot_table(\n",
    "    values='unemployment', index='growth_class', columns='continent',\n",
    "    aggfunc='mean', margins=True\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Avg unemployment by growth class × continent:')\n",
    "print(pivot_class.round(2).to_string())"
   ]
  },
