   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 6: Time Series — Econometric Patterns\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reference:** *Working with Time Series* (03.11) — DatetimeIndex, resampling, shifting, rolling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ── Convert to proper DatetimeIndex ──\n",
    "df_ts = df_analysis.copy()\n",
    "df_ts['date'] = pd.to_datetime(df_ts['year'], format='%Y')\n",
    "df_ts = df_ts.set_index('date').sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print('▼ Time-indexed DataFrame (USA subset):')\n",
    "print(df_ts[df_ts['country']=='USA'][['gdp_growth','unemployment','inflation']].to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Rolling mean: 3-year moving average smooths volatility ──\n",
    "df_ts['gdp_ma3'] = df_ts.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].transform(\n",
    "    lambda x: x.rolling(window=3, min_periods=1).mean()\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('\\n▼ 3-year moving average GDP growth (Japan):')\n",
    "jp = df_ts[df_ts['country']=='Japan'][['year','gdp_growth','gdp_ma3']]\n",
    "print(jp.round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Lag features for forecasting prep ──\n",
    "df_ts['gdp_lag1'] = df_ts.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].shift(1)\n",
    "df_ts['gdp_lag2'] = df_ts.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].shift(2)\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Lagged GDP values (China — first 4 years):')\n",
    "cn = df_ts[df_ts['country']=='China'][['year','gdp_growth','gdp_lag1','gdp_lag2']]\n",
    "print(cn.round(2).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Percentage change ──\n",
    "df_ts['gdp_pct_change'] = df_ts.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].pct_change()\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Year-over-year % change in GDP growth (Germany):')\n",
    "de = df_ts[df_ts['country']=='Germany'][['year','gdp_growth','gdp_pct_change']]\n",
    "print(de.round(3).to_string())\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Period filtering: post-pandemic recovery ──\n",
    "post_covid = df_ts.loc['2020-01-01':]\n",
    "print('\\n▼ Post-2020 average GDP growth by country:')\n",
    "print(post_covid.groupby('country')['gdp_growth'].mean().round(2).sort_values(ascending=False).to_string())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Insight ▸** Rolling averages smooth out short-term noise — essential for identifying underlying economic trends. Lag features are the foundation of autoregressive forecasting models (ARIMA, VAR)."
   ]
